<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέμβ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, a ship's
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cock-boat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				32.6
			</span></i>: metaph., of a <i>parasite</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄπισθεν ἀκολουθεῖ κόλαξ τῳ; λέμβος
					ἐπικέκληται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					34.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fishingboat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				21.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fast-sailing galley, felucca</i>, used either to precede a
			fleet, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.53.9
			</span></i>; or as a light transport, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.3.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.109.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				569.19
			</span></i> (Halasarna, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				2p.64
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
